<!--
  Synthetic C-CDA Encounters section. No patient data.

  The narrative table is ordered Date, Type, Department, Care Team,
  Description, so reading it by position (date, type, provider, chief
  complaint, assessment) stores the department as the provider and the care
  team as the chief complaint. The entries carry every field explicitly:

    enc-display      CPT code with a displayName; start and end times; a
                     performer with a specialty; a service location; an
                     indication; an encounter diagnosis with an ICD-10-CM
                     translation
    enc-original     ActCode whose originalText references the narrative cell;
                     a date without a time; only an organization performs it
    enc-code-only    nothing but the CPT code names its type
    enc-planned      moodCode INT: planned, not happened

  enc-display and enc-original reference their rows.
-->
